WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.990
. Hey, David, Joe Biden keeps talking about
compromising with Republicans and working

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.160
across the aisle.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.940
Is Biden nuts for thinking this Republican
Party will compromise with him?

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.280
Well, this this requires some speculation
about what Biden actually thinks and believes.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.490
What I mean by that is I don't know that Joe
Biden really thinks this Republican Party

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.619
is going to work with him.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.810
And in fact, I doubt he thinks that.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:26.519
I believe Joe Biden is talking about reaching
across the aisle and getting Republicans to

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:31.859
compromise because he's trying to be a unifying
figure who at least appears willing to reach

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:32.859
out to.

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:38.220
Republican voters, it makes them look presidential,
it appeals to more than just the Democratic

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.950
Party and it in a way puts pressure on Republicans.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:43.950
Many are friends with Biden.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:48.640
Remember, Biden has a lot of Republican friends
to try to rise above partizanship.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:55.820
But my belief is Biden knows, especially because
they've been clear Republicans will be obstructionist

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:01.180
buffoons for the next at least two years,
likely for they will try to get in the way

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.660
of any accomplishment that the Democratic
Party tries to do.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:12.960
And so I don't believe Joe Biden's rhetoric
about bipartisanship and compromise will go

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:13.960
anywhere.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:19.360
I think with this Republican Party, the only
the only way to get them to work with Biden

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.300
would be to make such significant concessions
that these legislative victories would end

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.680
up being Pyrrhic victories.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:33.080
In other words, victories in which you you
you are so much damage is inflicted upon you

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.990
that you start to wonder, is it really even
a victory in the net?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:42.960
So I think, you know, if I believed Biden
naively believed Mitch McConnell is going

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.900
to help him get the tax reform done that he
wants, and the public option of that would

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.380
be insanely naive of Joe Biden.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.700
But I don't think he believes that.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.570
I believe it's mostly posturing.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:59.020
I believe Joe Biden knows because Republicans
have made it clear they will obstruct absolutely

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.240
everything that they can.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.170
And I'm not particularly optimistic that Republicans
are going to participate in anything over

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.170
the next four years.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.069
So what can Joe Biden get done without Republicans?

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:15.420
What can Joe Biden get done with executive
orders?

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.640
It remains to be seen and will be here for
the ride.

